## Local secrets / env (never commit)
*.env
.env
# A dated or suffixed copy of an env file carries the same secrets as the original, and the
# patterns above match neither (".env.bak.20260918" ends in a date, not in ".env").
.env.*
*.env.*
appsettings.*.local.json
secrets.json

## SQLFlow run artifacts, model state, and local secrets (.sqlflow/env)
.sqlflow/

## Docker sample-data dumps (fetched on demand by docker/fetch-samples; hand-written init scripts stay tracked)
docker/mysql/initdb/*.sql
docker/postgres/initdb/*.sql
docker/oracle/sakila-sql/*.sql

## GUI local run logs and e2e artifacts (generated when running the control plane / Playwright locally)
gui/control-plane.log
gui/control-plane.err.log
gui/e2e-node.log
gui/e2e-run.log
gui/e2e-artifacts/

## Acquisition engine runtime-landed raw files
_landing/

# Clean build contexts produced by deploy-prod.ps1 (git-archive extracts)
.deploy-ctx/

# The TypeScript incremental-build cache: pure build output that every typecheck rewrites, so tracking it
# dirties the tree on any machine that builds the GUI.
gui/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

## Coding-agent working files (local to a checkout, never part of the product)
.claude/
AGENTS.md
.cursor/
.aider*

## Power BI sample reports: the binary .pbix files are large and are not the product.
## The extracted *.spec.yaml specifications ARE tracked, since they are reviewable text.
samples/powerbi/*.pbix

## Manual PowerAI test estate (throwaway, not part of the product)
.powerai-manual-test/

## Local MCP client registration: points at a developer's own control plane and can carry a live bearer token
.mcp.json
